\f1\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 Long-Term Goal\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Rather than being \'93just another security scanner,\'94 Aegis X would become a 
\f1\b \cf2 \strokec2 developer security platform
\f0\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  that:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Protects local projects.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Protects Git repositories.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Verifies build artifacts.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Improves software supply-chain security.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Integrates with editors, CI/CD systems, and developer workflows.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Provides reusable libraries and APIs for other applications.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 That\'92s an ambitious but technically achievable vision if it\'92s built incrementally with a strong core and clear module boundaries. The next practical step is to create the Rust workspace, define the kernel interfaces, and get the first CLI command (
\f2 \cf2 \strokec2 aegis init
\f0 \cf2 \strokec2 ) working end to end before adding more advanced capabilities.\
